 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Ddi4JBaNoCM/",
 "title": "Your Product is Not the Hero",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator claims that making the brand or product the hero of the story is the biggest storytelling mistake businesses make. The core lesson is that the customer must be the hero, while the product is merely the enabler of their success.",
 "key_points": [
  "The single biggest storytelling mistake brands make is making themselves the hero of the story.",
  "Brands often focus on statements like we launched this, or we are the fastest, smartest, or largest.",
  "Customers do not wake up wanting to be part of a company's story.",
  "Customers want a better version of their own story, such as a problem solved, frustration removed, concern conquered, or life made easier.",
  "Your product simply serves as the enabler to that change.",
  "Stop putting your brand center stage because the hero of your story is always your customer."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Chris Hewitt. Text / caption: The single biggest mistake I see in brand storytelling and how to fix it, fast #brandstorytelling #businessstorytelling #personalbrand. Transcript: Oh sorry if you don't want to hear this, but your product is not the hero. Your brand is not the hero. Sorry, but it is not. And it is probably the single biggest storytelling mistake that I see brands making today. They always make themselves to be the hero of the story. We've launched this; we're the market leader that; we're the fastest, the smartest, the largest, we're the healthiest, whatever it is. But nobody wakes up in the morning wanting to be part of your company's story. They want a better version of their own story, a problem solved, a frustration removed, a concern conquered, a life made easier. Your product simply is the enabler to that change. So stop putting your brand center stage, because the hero of your story is not you, it is always your customer. My name is Chris here, chief storyteller here at Barkley Communications. Follow me for more tips.",
